{{Term/Store|Islander Hawk|Islander Hawks|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium"/><ref name="ToTK Hyrule Compendium"/>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Islander Hawk}}
Islander Hawks are carnivorous [[Bird]]s that can be found flying in [[Hyrule Field]] and [[Hyrule Ridge]].<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium 2"/> Their diet consists of smaller [[Creature]]s and other Birds, which they search for while flying in the sky.<ref name="BotW Hyrule Compendium 2"/> Like most Birds, they can be hunted by [[Link]] for [[Food]], dropping [[Raw Bird Thigh]]s when killed.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Islander Hawk}}
Islander Hawks reappear in {{TotK}}.

==Nomenclature==
Islander Hawk may be a mistranslation of its Japanese name, {{Romanize|シマオタカ|Shimao Taka}}, which is supposedly spelled {{Romanize|縞尾鷹|Shima O Taka|stripe-tailed hawk|2}}, as the animals in {{BotW|-}} and {{TotK|-}} are named in a style that is similar to {{Wp|ja:和名|Wamei}}, a standardized name of a species in Japanese.
